From 89560c6f7dbdeca83199c62dc5a9c4ec1a3d56f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:32:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: fp8 KV cache (--kv-cache fp8) for K and V
 pages

K and V become e4m3 rows with one fp32 scale per token and kv head (rule of
kv_fp8.cuh: scale amax / 448 floored at 2^-126, saturating nearest-even codes,
a row with a NaN or infinity stores a NaN scale); the index keys stay bf16.
47,040 B a token a rank instead of 76,800; 128-token page 6,021,120 B instead
of 9,830,400.

tf_mm3_rows (flags bit 64), tf_mm3_attn and tf_mm3_index (trailing kv8
parameter) take the mode as a launch parameter; the bf16 paths are unchanged
and the default. Options.kv8 lets the host's refusal pass the flag; Dims,
PageMap, Paged, the budget and the layout follow; Settings.kv8 is in the ranks'
fingerprint. minimax_ref.zig gets the float64 quantizer and attention over fp8
K/V; test-minimax-kv8 holds host twins with planted mutants; mm3-contract gains
fp8 writer and attention variants (not run on a GPU).

No GPU run. The effect of fp8 K/V on the model's answers is not measured.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
